       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline has no recognized indication at 1000 mg/day. Doses above 200 mg/day add no benefit and substantially raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. If a patient received this dose daily, I'd expect real harm. You also haven't given a clinical reason for it, so I think it's more likely a slip than a deliberate choice.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** Tell me 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily and I'll place it.\n- **Help with a different problem.** If the goal is to treat a refractory case, I can enter an adjunct or a switch to another agent. A psychiatry or pharmacy consult might also help.\n- **Route a true outlier dose through pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for 1000 mg, such as a protocol or a toxicology plan, it should go through a pharmacy-verified override process. I can't do that for you from here.\n\nWhich would you like?"
